  Pattern Comparison

  ✅ Correct (pkg/bus/bus.go):
  type InProcBus struct {
      tracer tracing.Tracer  // Field in struct
  }
  func ProvideBus(tracer tracing.Tracer) *InProcBus {  // DI constructor
      return &InProcBus{tracer: tracer}
  }
  func (b *InProcBus) Publish(ctx) {
      _, span := b.tracer.Start(ctx, ...)  // Use via receiver
  }

  ❌ Incorrect (pkg/api/api.go, pkg/services/accesscontrol/accesscontrol.go):
  var tracer = otel.Tracer("github.com/grafana/grafana/pkg/api")
  // ...
  _, span := tracer.Start(ctx, ...)  // Direct global usage

  Why It Matters

  - Global tracers are untestable (can't inject mocks)
  - Implicit dependencies vs. explicit Wire DI
  - Inconsistent with Grafana's architecture patterns

  The migration is straightforward for each file: add a tracer field to the struct, include it in the constructor, and replace all tracer.Start() calls with s.tracer.Start().

